SUMMARY:Agiasos Carnival (Agiasotiki Apokria)
LOCATION:Agiasos\, Lesvos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The most literary carnival in the Aegean: the 'Satyros' carnival society of Agiasos writes satirical verse in the local dialect\, performs it in the streets and runs masked parties\, a children's masquerade and a 'patinada' with traditional musicians on Carnival Sunday\, all culminating on Clean Monday with kites\, free bean soup and rice pudding and the big satirical procession. Runs the last two weekends before Lent\; the Monday is the day to be there.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lesvos/#agiasos-agiasos-carnival-agiasotiki-apokria
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lesvos/#agiasos-agiasos-carnival-agiasotiki-apokria
